### Description

Launch an existing job plan. The API returns the job instance ID synchronously, which can be used to query the execution status and logs.

Before calling: the target job plan must exist and the caller must have the permission to view and launch that job plan in the resource scope.

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| bk_scope_type | string | Yes | Resource scope type. Options: `biz` (business), `biz_set` (business set) |
| bk_scope_id | string | Yes | Resource scope ID, corresponding to `bk_scope_type`, that is the business ID or the business set ID |
| job_plan_id | long | Yes | ID of the job plan to launch |
| global_var_list | array | No | Global variable values. All default values defined in the job plan are used when omitted |
| callback_url | string | No | Callback URL invoked after the job finishes, at most 1024 characters. Job calls it once the job completes |
| start_task | boolean | No | Whether to start the job immediately. Options: `true` (start immediately, the default), `false` (only create the job instance without starting it, which can be started later via the job instance operation API) |

##### global_var_list[] element

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| id | long | No | Global variable ID. Provide either `id` or `name`; this one wins if both are given |
| name | string | No | Global variable name. Provide either `id` or `name` |
| value | string | No | Global variable value. Use `execute_target` for execution target variables, and this field for the other types (string, namespace, ciphertext, associative array, indexed array) |
| execute_target | object | No | Value of an execution target type global variable |

##### execute_target

{% include '_generic_v4_execute_target.md.j2' %}

**Note:** Hosts and containers cannot be mixed in one execution.

